From: ricktav <82380971+ricktav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:52:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: apple: Probe the A7 (S5L8960X) GPU

The A7's G6430 (Apple's G3) runs a META LDR firmware like the A8 and A9,
but the A7's core revision, PLL lock bit, bus bridge settings and
firmware layout are not known yet. Match "apple,s5l8960x-gpu" with a chip
that stops the probe with -ENODEV before any of that, so the node, its
power domain and the firmware's file name are in place for the work that
follows.

By default the probe touches no GPU register. powervr.apple_a7_read_id=1
wakes Fender into state 1 with an empty boot stream, as the A8 driver does
before its ID read, logs CORE_REVISION and CORE_ID and puts Fender back
to state 0: the first measurement on hardware, which may hang the SoC.

Assisted-by: LLM
